      "content": "that makes sense from a statistical standpoint. but i want to dig a bit deeper into the logic of the simulation. \n\nwhen the model calculates that risk for District B, how much weight is being placed on the racial demographic specifically versus the income level? like, if we kept the income and density the same but swapped the demographics—so District B was mostly white but still low-income—would the \"risk\" score stay the same, or does the racial makeup itself act as a predictive factor in these types of models?",
